<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asander (Bosporan king)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 17 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asander was ruler of the Bosporan Kingdom from 47 BCE until about 17 BCE. Left in charge of the Bosporus by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharnaces-ii-of-pontus">Pharnaces II</a>, he rebelled against him, and after Pharnaces' defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zela">Zela</a> he fought and killed him and seized power, marrying Pharnaces' daughter Dynamis to strengthen his claim. Recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, he first ruled as archon and later as king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asander-bosporan-king.jpg" alt="Asander (Bosporan king)" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:LouisAragon (uploader) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_coin_of_Asander_as_King_of_the_Bosporan_Kingdom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
